[TEXT] **Root cause confirmed.** Router6's nftables FORWARD chain contains blocking rules on `iifname "eth2"` (the backbone link to router3):

```
iifname "eth2" ip saddr 172.16.10.0/24 ip daddr 172.18.51.1 tcp dport 80 → ACCEPT  (single exception)
iifname "eth2" meta l4proto tcp  → DROP  (21+ packets)
iifname "eth2" meta l4proto udp  → DROP
iifname "eth2"                   → DROP  (51+ packets — catches ICMP and everything else)
```

- IP forwarding is enabled (`net.ipv4.ip_forward = 1`) — router6 is not misconfigured at the kernel level
- Router6 can directly ping pc18 (172.18.51.18) and router3 (10.50.1.1) — local L2 and L3 are fine
- But **all forwarded traffic arriving from eth2 (the backbone) is dropped** — inbound routing from outside the 172.18.50/51.0/24 domain is dead
